---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { getPath } from '../../utils/paths';
import versionsData from '../../data/versions.json';

const activeRelease = versionsData.broker?.activeRelease || 'v0.5.3';

const runCommand = `# 1. Initialize KRaft metadata on a fresh storage volume
docker run --rm \\
  -v krabka-data:/var/lib/krabka \\
  ghcr.io/krabka-io/krabka-broker:latest \\
  /usr/bin/krabka-format \\
  --log-dir=/var/lib/krabka \\
  --standalone \\
  --node-id=1 \\
  --controller-listener=localhost:9093

# 2. Run the broker daemon
docker run -d \\
  --name krabka \\
  -p 9092:9092 \\
  -v krabka-data:/var/lib/krabka \\
  ghcr.io/krabka-io/krabka-broker:latest \\
  --listen-addr=0.0.0.0:9092 \\
  --advertised-listener=localhost:9092 \\
  --log-dir=/var/lib/krabka \\
  --process-roles=controller,broker`;

const brokerCrates = [
  { name: 'krabka-broker', desc: 'Request handlers, coordinators, partition replication, quotas, server binary' },
  { name: 'krabka-raft', desc: 'KRaft consensus engine implementing KIP-595 wire RPC protocol' },
  { name: 'krabka-kraft-core', desc: 'Shared KRaft record types and quorum state machine' },
  { name: 'krabka-log', desc: 'On-disk write-ahead log: segments, index files, compaction, retention' },
  { name: 'krabka-logfmt', desc: 'High-performance binary log record formatter and framing' },
  { name: 'krabka-remote-storage', desc: 'Tiered-storage reader and cloud object storage offloader' },
  { name: 'krabka-remote-storage-topic', desc: 'The __remote_log_metadata topic-backed RLMM' },
  { name: 'krabka-object-store', desc: 'Unified asynchronous cloud object store driver (S3, GCS, MinIO, Azure Blob)' },
  { name: 'krabka-verified', desc: 'Formally verified core arithmetic, compaction, and recovery algorithms with Creusot proofs' },
  { name: 'krabka-throttle', desc: 'Token-bucket rate limiters and KIP-scoped client quota enforcement' },
  { name: 'krabka-authz', desc: 'Authorizer traits, ACL evaluations, and OPA client' },
  { name: 'krabka-audit', desc: 'Security audit events, OCSF serialization, and verify CLI' },
  { name: 'krabka-format', desc: 'Formats fresh log directory: meta.properties.json and VotersRecord' },
  { name: 'krabka-restore', desc: 'Snapshot compaction and disaster recovery utilities' },
  { name: 'krabka-records-legacy', desc: 'V0 and V1 legacy message format codecs and downconversion' },
  { name: 'krabka-telemetry', desc: 'OTLP pipeline, Prometheus metrics, and pprof debug endpoints' },
  { name: 'krabka-barrier', desc: 'Distributed barrier alignment CLI utility' },
  { name: 'krabka-guard', desc: 'Mutants and invariant verification test harness CLI' },
  { name: 'krabka-parse-benches', desc: 'Microbenchmarking parse harnesses and latency profiles' },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Broker Engine Overview (krabka-broker)"
  description="Architecture, request handling pipeline, storage layout, and KRaft consensus in the Krabka broker."
  currentSlug="/docs/broker"
>
  <div class="space-y-6 font-sans">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="border-b border-white/10 pb-4 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-4">
      <div>
        <div class="text-xs text-gray-400 mb-1">
          Rust Edition 2024 · Release {activeRelease}
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-white sm:text-4xl">Broker Engine Overview</h1>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mt-2 text-sm max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
          The core streaming broker: request pipelines, write-ahead logs, coordinators, and KRaft consensus via <code>krabka-broker</code>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <a
        href={getPath('/api/broker/latest/')}
        class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg bg-krab-500/20 hover:bg-krab-500/30 border border-krab-500/40 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-krab-300 hover:text-white transition-colors shrink-0"
      >
        Browse Rustdoc Reference
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-sm text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        <code>krabka-broker</code> is a native Rust, byte-exact drop-in replacement for Apache Kafka. It runs without the JVM, using asynchronous I/O and direct kernel memory management for zero-copy record batching.
      </p>

      <!-- Architecture & Engineering Guides -->
      <div class="space-y-3 pt-2">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Architecture & Engineering Guides</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-300 mt-1">
            In-depth technical guides maintained alongside the broker codebase:
          </p>
        </div>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-300 list-disc pl-5 marker:text-krab-400">
          <li>
            <a href={getPath('/docs/broker/config-reference')} class="font-semibold text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300 hover:underline transition-colors">Broker Configuration Reference:</a> Comprehensive server properties, listener parameters, and storage thresholds.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href={getPath('/docs/broker/verification')} class="font-semibold text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300 hover:underline transition-colors">Verification & Invariants:</a> Formal mathematical proofs with Creusot and model checking with Stateright.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href={getPath('/docs/broker/kip_matrix')} class="font-semibold text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300 hover:underline transition-colors">Kafka KIP Compatibility Matrix:</a> Kafka Improvement Proposals implementation status and behavioral conformance.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href={getPath('/docs/broker/docgen-contract')} class="font-semibold text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300 hover:underline transition-colors">Docgen Contract:</a> Compiler-enforced doc generation contracts and JSON schema synchronizers.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href={getPath('/docs/broker/releasing')} class="font-semibold text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300 hover:underline transition-colors">Release Process:</a> Build verification steps, SLSA Level 3 provenance attestations, and release signing.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Quickstart Running Broker -->
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Running a Broker</h2>
      <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl p-5 border border-white/10 space-y-3">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-gray-400">
          <span>Docker Run (Single-Node KRaft)</span>
          <button type="button" class="copy-btn rounded bg-white/5 px-2 py-1 text-gray-300 hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-white transition-colors text-xs" data-copy={runCommand}>
            Copy
          </button>
        </div>
        <pre class="bg-black/50 p-4 rounded-lg font-mono text-xs text-gray-200 overflow-x-auto border border-white/5"><code>{runCommand}</code></pre>
      </div>

      <!-- Published Crates Table -->
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Broker Crates & Subsystems</h2>
      <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-white/10">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border-collapse">
          <thead class="bg-slate-950/80 border-b border-white/10 uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-400 font-semibold">
            <tr>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Crate</th>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Purpose & Subsystem</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
            {brokerCrates.map((c) => {
              const crateFolder = c.name.replace(/^krabka-/, '');
              const githubUrl = `https://github.com/krabka-io/krabka-broker/tree/main/crates/${crateFolder}#readme`;
              return (
                <tr class="hover:bg-white/5 transition-colors">
                  <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium">
                    <a
                      href={githubUrl}
                      target="_blank"
                      rel="noopener noreferrer"
                      class="text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300 hover:underline transition-colors"
                    >
                      {c.name}
                    </a>
                  </td>
                  <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-400">{c.desc}</td>
                </tr>
              );
            })}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <!-- Version & Compatibility Reference -->
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Version & Compatibility</h2>
      <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-white/10">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border-collapse">
          <thead class="bg-slate-950/80 border-b border-white/10 uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-400 font-semibold">
            <tr>
              <th class="py-2.5 px-4">Component</th>
              <th class="py-2.5 px-4">Supported Version</th>
              <th class="py-2.5 px-4">Notes</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-white/5 text-gray-300">
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2 px-4 font-medium text-white">Rust Toolchain</td>
              <td class="py-2 px-4">Rust 1.97.1+ (Edition 2024)</td>
              <td class="py-2 px-4 text-gray-400">Nightly required for formal verification passes</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2 px-4 font-medium text-white">Kafka Wire Protocol</td>
              <td class="py-2 px-4">Kafka 4.3.1 (KIP-595 KRaft)</td>
              <td class="py-2 px-4 text-gray-400">Byte-exact request/response schema serialization</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2 px-4 font-medium text-white">OS Architecture</td>
              <td class="py-2 px-4">Linux x86_64, aarch64</td>
              <td class="py-2 px-4 text-gray-400">glibc 2.35+ or musl</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-300">
        Full version matrices and SLSA Level 3 build provenance records are tracked on the <a href={getPath('/versions')} class="text-krab-400 hover:underline">Versions page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Related Resources</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 not-prose pt-1">
        <a href={getPath('/docs/benchmarks')} class="p-4 rounded-xl frosted-card border border-white/10 hover:border-krab-500/50 transition-colors block">
          <div class="text-sm font-bold text-white">Benchmark Methodology →</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1">Direct I/O NVMe throughput, memory RSS, and latency profiles vs Strimzi Kafka.</p>
        </a>
        <a href={getPath('/docs/runtime-architecture')} class="p-4 rounded-xl frosted-card border border-white/10 hover:border-krab-500/50 transition-colors block">
          <div class="text-sm font-bold text-white">Runtime Architecture →</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1">Operational topology, internal broker components, and control plane reconcile loops.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
